{"name":"Knights of the Desert","hex":"#403c39","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of knight"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of knight"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knights"},{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knights of the Desert","blocks":[{"text":"Knights of the Desert is a 1983 computer wargame developed by Tactical Design Group and published by Strategic Simulations for the Apple II, Atari 8-bit computers, Commodore 64, MS-DOS, and TRS-80. It is based on the 1940-43 North African campaign."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Knights_of_the_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Desert","wikidata":"Q6422504"},{"title":"Knights of the Desert (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Knights of the Desert is a 1942 Italian adventure film directed by Gino Talamo and Osvaldo Valenti. It starred Valenti, Luisa Ferida and Luigi Pavese. The film was based on a novel by Emilio Salgari with a screenplay by Federico Fellini and Vittorio Mussolini, the son of Italy's dictator Benito Mussolini. It was produced by the Rome-based ACI which was run by Vittorio Mussolini. Valenti and Ferida were romantically linked, and co-starred in several films together."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Desert_(film)","wikidata":"Q3790607"},{"title":"Knight","blocks":[{"text":"A knight is a person granted an honorary title of a knighthood by a head of state or representative for service to the monarch, the church, or the country, especially in a military capacity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg/330px-Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight","wikidata":"Q102083"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert","wikidata":"Q8514"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/Knights_of_the_Desert_Atari_8-bit_PAL_screenshot.png/330px-Knights_of_the_Desert_Atari_8-bit_PAL_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/Knights_of_the_Desert_Atari_8-bit_PAL_screenshot.png/330px-Knights_of_the_Desert_Atari_8-bit_PAL_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gameplay screenshot (Atari 8-bit)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o